======================================================================
ORIGIN of j->6-j reflection, and exact rational character pieces
======================================================================
Explanation: tau->1-tau is a measure-preserving involution of [0,1)
  sending sector j -> sector 6-j. So q_j=q_{6-j} EXACTLY (real-analytic reality).


NOTE: j->6-j sends j=6 -> 0 (the ANCHOR sector). So the additive reflection
does NOT preserve {1..6}. The multiplicative inversion j->-j=7-j sends 6->1 etc.
These differ. The TRUE reality of q is the ADDITIVE reflection about 3.
Let me recheck: is q ALSO invariant under multiplicative inversion j->7-j?
  E=[0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7]: q[7-j]=q[j] (mult inversion)? False
  E=[0, 1, 2, 4]: q[7-j]=q[j] (mult inversion)? False

======================================================================
RIGHT OBJECT: multiplicative-character decomposition needs a MULT-equivariant input.
The single-sector miss q_j is ADDITIVELY symmetric (j->6-j), NOT mult (j->-j).
So mult-char mass on q is spread. Test the FULL sieve p0 and the M7 main term.
