======================================================================
THE DECORRELATED MOD-7 KERNEL D7 and its 6-character spectrum
======================================================================
KEY: p0(aE)=p0(E) for all a in (Z/7)* (exact). Hence for any nontrivial chi_k:
   sum_{a} chi_k(a) p0(aE) = p0(E) sum_a chi_k(a) = 0.
   => p0 is a PURELY TRIVIAL-CHARACTER (chi_0) object under dilation.
   The cube-root/sign/order-6 pieces of p0-under-dilation all VANISH identically.

So the mult-character mass of the COVERAGE itself sits 100% in chi_0 (trivial).
The C_3 and sign structure appears only when we BREAK dilation invariance, i.e.
inside the SECTOR-RESOLVED miss vector q_j (which is additively, not mult, symmetric).

======================================================================
WHERE C_3 AND SIGN LIVE: dilation acts on sector-SUBSETS S of {1..6}.
p0 = sum_S (-1)^|S| m_S. Group the 2^6 subsets of {1..6} into (Z/7)*-orbits.
Within each orbit, m_{aS}(E)=m_S(a^{-1}E); summed against chi_k gives the kernel.
